  "_comment": [
    "80% looks alarming and is honest: the rule requires a member to be cited in the SAME code span as its own type, and most reference prose writes `result.code` without repeating `ActionResult` nearby. Tightening the docs to satisfy it is real work; the ratchet is what makes that work optional today and impossible to regress.",
    "Generated baseline, not a target. Regenerate intentionally, never to silence a failure.",
    "`enforced` pins every Type.member pair the gate checks, so a rename or a dropped type shows up as a reviewable diff instead of silently shrinking the gate.",
    "`undocumented` is the debt as of the day this landed. The gate fails on a member that is NEWLY undocumented, and also fails if an entry here becomes documented, so the list can only shrink."
  ]
}
